"# Time to look at what Mortimer has written\nI didn’t do it yesterday\nFrom what I can see in the previews, she circles back to her larger points it looks like\\.\n\n---\n\n> this isn't a direct response, it's a remembered thing, hence no \\.\\.\\.whatever it's called\\. reply thingy\\.\n> \n> Okay first of all going back to the teeth comment and you occasionally just saying mean things, I remembered the recent example I was thinking of, but then couldn’t remember at the time\\. It was the hair thing on my birthday\\. After Jill had left and we were still talking and I was saying how I was paranoid that, even though that isn’t how hair or genetics works, my hair just wasn’t curly anymore because it still didn’t look curly and it was freaking me out etc\\., and for some reason you said ‘you know what would be funny? If your hair was just straight now\\.’ and, like, I went along with it because I didn’t want to make it A Thing, particularly on my birthday since I was having a good day/pretty good stretch of days etc\\. And I meant to bring it up after, but xmas and everything meant I kept forgetting\\. I did mention it to Dorian though because I was like “yo wtf, how is that funny?” and also kind of upset about it tbh\\.\n> And\\. Admittedly\\. Passive aggressively in the group chat the other day\\. I think I was just in a mood, but I also kinda think I wanted you to realize on your own that it was a weird, not\\-very\\-nice thing to say and apologize on your own time without me having to bring it up and make it A Thing\\.\n\nOh, I see\\.\nYou’re very right\\.\nI should have apologized on my own for that one\\.\nI’m sorry\\.\n\n---\n\nReplying to:\n> Hmm\\. I get that\\. I do\\.\n> I\\.\\.\\. I don’t know\\. I do honestly think that I understand what you mean, what it is to you\\.\\.\\.\\.\n\n> Yes, but it’s the fact that you were still saying that I don’t *really* care etc\\. is what I am getting at\\. You understand what I’m saying, but I do not think you understand it as a whole\\. Because at no point have you said that you understand that it is me actually caring \\(albeit not about the thing directly that much\\), and to me that says that, although you are comprehending the words, understanding the concept in a general sense, you don’t actually understand the feeling\\. Which also makes me think that, on some level, you are still always going to feel some level of insincerity and/or hollowness\\.\n\nHmm\\. Interesting\\.\nThe trouble here is, I’ve kind of lost touch with how I was thinking and feeling when I was talking about those feelings and ideas\\.\nSo now I’m at a point where I’m\\.\\.\\. for lack of better phrasing, fully onboard with what you’re saying, and wondering if maybe I was just entertaining and communicating knee\\-jerk feelings that I should have sat with a little more\\.\nI mean\\.\\.\\.\nI don’t know\\.\nBecause maybe not\\.\nFor me, I think\\.\\.\\.\\. I think “understanding you fully, understanding your care fully” and “being aware that your interest isn’t directly in the thing being talked about” aren’t mutually exclusive\\.\nI think that the latter doesn’t mean I’m actually thinking you’re insincere and hollow\\.\nMaybe it just means I feel bad that you’re engaging and putting in this effort and I\\.\\.\\. just don’t really know how to do that\\.\nBecause the longer we discuss that, the more that’s where I end up: Yes, you’re right, I should be actively providing you that engagement\\. And I just don’t really know how\\.\n\n---\n\nReplying to:\n> Hmm\\. Fair enough, I guess\\.\n> Need to go back and look at what you’re referring to with “idealizing”\\.\\.\\.\\.\\.\n\n> specifically\n> \n> ”But I do think there’s a pretty reasonable difference between the two, and I don’t think I’m out of line for acknowledging it and wondering what I’m supposed to make of it\\.”\n> \n> I… never said it was unreasonable? In fact, I think I was agreeing that it was a reasonable question, and then  just explaining why I think there was such a disparity? I don’t really understand where you got the implication I was saying it was wrong of you to be confused?\n> \n> I mean\\. The second response is also unfiltered, I just wasn’t as worked up? Also, I am not classifying having varied opinions based on current emotion as an autism thing, I was classifying the whole deal of being so strongly influenced in the moment, but also in a way you yourself cannot fully understand\\. Because I do think that is an autism thing, as it relates to the tendency in autistic people to struggle with identifying emotions and really pinpointing and clearly defining them, etc\\.\n> And that is something that I already knew I struggled with, but have also realized more and more since having an official diagnosis \\(and subsequently feeling more able to relate to research/accounts by autistic people without the fear of someone \\(who? idk\\) saying I’m, like, faking it or co\\-opting something blah blah weird gatekeep\\-y health bullcannoli\\)\\.\n> I\\. Hm\\. It’s maybe too nuanced and personal for me to even be able to explain to you exactly what I mean about how/why me saying that I think it is an autistic/neurodivergent thing is most likely accurate, so, I don’t know\\. I guess it is up to you whether or not you believe it\\.\n\n> I… never said it was unreasonable?\nI mean, unless I misunderstood the “idealizing” bit, you explicitly objected to it\\. “I don’t appreciate you implying\\.\\.\\.”, etc\\. You objected to what I was saying, so I defended it here\\.\n\nBut for the rest of it, fair enough\\.\n\n---\n\nReplying to:\n> Okay, so I’m not saying either way you expressed your feelings was wrong or a lie\\.\\.\\.\n\n> “Well, yes\\. Sure, yeah, I guess\\. I just\\.\\.\\. I think there’s\\.\\.\\. I think there’s a medium, right? This will be supported more later on, but There’s the “within reason” bar that you don’t go beyond\\.”\n> \n> Uh\\. Yeah? Sure? I mean there are always limits to things, obviously\\. I\\. Look, I’m sorry, but I just like… don’t want to spend more of my energy on explaining the Frodoe thing again? I mean, I’m not saying don’t talk about it\\. Do, by all means\\. I am just saying that I still disagree with you about this in some way\\(s\\)/on some level\\(s\\)\\. Saying the Frodoe thing to me over and over isn’t going to change my opinion, and I’m not even trying to change yours, I was/am just trying to explain to you the way I see things\\. So at this point, I think I have a pretty good understanding of how you see it, and I think you have a decent understanding of how I see it, and I think we just\\. Disagree\\.\n> To me, it’s an insult how little of the things I’m interested in trying/doing/whatever you are willing to even consider trying\\. Not everything, of course, that wouldn’t be fair\\. Like\\. I don’t think I’m as unreasonable as you think I am about this? But then again, I think you’re the one with the unreasonable decision\\. And honestly, I kind of think most people would agree? But then again, does that Morker? I suppose not\\. You’re you and that’s that, and that’s fine\\. I’m me and I disagree with you on this, and that’s fine too\\. I dunno what else to say about it anymore\\.\n\n> I was/am just trying to explain to you the way I see things\nAs am I\\.\nAnd I think the short version, in the context of this message, is that I think that there aren’t actually all that many things that you want me to try that I don’t, and I think if you start breaking them down, you get a lot of things that aren’t truly that big of a deal, that aren’t worth creating conflict over, and I think you get a lot of things where there’s more to it than just “Arnie the Donut is being a brat who doesn’t want to try new things”\\. \\(For lack of better phrasing \\- there’s no need to call out my use of the word “brat” here\\.\\)\nI think context is everything, and there are two sides to all of these things\\.\n\n---\n\n> and again, not a direct response to anything, just my final thoughts as of right now or whatever idk\n\n---\n\n> At the end of the day, a lot of what my original List of Gripes \\(as I have been calling it in my head\\) comes down to is that I don’t think you put in an equal amount of effort/energy into us as a couple\\. Your responses and reactions to things, ultimately, suggest to me that those things aren’t going to change\\. Honestly I think I have kind of known since you last visited that things were donked\\. Well, okay, I think on some level I have known for a long time, but I think it’s been since your last visit that it has finally clawed its way out of my subconscious\\. I’m sorry, to both of us, that it took me so long to figure it out\\. I do think things work a lot better for us in person, or at least the pros far more heavily outweigh the cons then, but… I don’t know\\. You’ve kept putting off looking for a place, and in a lot of respects I understand the reasons why, but I also think a lot of it is just… treading water? I don’t know\\. I’ve been really depressed since you last left and I have spent a lot of time wondering why, and I kind of think I’ve been grieving? I love you a lot, I really do\\. I think you’re great, and I think I’m lucky to have met you and I appreciate you putting up with me and calling me out for cannoli and I honestly think things could work out really well if we were “in person,” but the way things are going I don’t think we are ever going to get there\\. I know you keep saying we will and soon, but you’ve been saying that for nearly five years\\. And who knows, maybe we have corrupted each other’s personalities so much at this point that we really are stuck together, like I used to always joke about, and we’ll pick back up some time in the future when I am \\(hopefully please please dear sweet any deities please\\) back in New England, but it definitely isn’t working at the moment\\. And that’s okay\\. I mean sure, the thought has been making me feel sick to my stomach regularly all week, but I think it has to be done\\. If nothing else, I think we just need time to be our own people for a while after being together for so long since we were so young, you know?\n> I dunno, I think at this point I am saying stuff more for my own comfort than yours\\.\n> Also, just to clarify, because you know I love to “clarify,” I’m not even saying this in a “well we need to see other people and maybe it will turn out we were the better match for each other” or anything? Like\\. I just\\. Know I need space\\. Which is also why I think I eventually put together what was happening after you left, because as much fun as I had while you were here, I just kept finding myself feeling irritated with you afterwards\\. You weren’t even doing anything, but I just kept feeling irritated, and I kept thinking of things that bothered me, etc\\., and I don’t like that\\. I don’t want to be like that\\. It was making me feel like I was being really snappy \\(I don’t know if I actually was, half out of forgetfulness and half out of knowing I tend to feel I’m being snappy before anyone else ever thinks I am being snappy\\), and that isn’t fair to you, and I don’t want to get to a point where I resent you, especially since it would have been for no reason, you know? That’s why I was like hey maybe we don’t need to talk every day, etc\\. And in and of itself, I think that’s fine; I don’t know why or how we did talk every single day for so long, but I think the fact that I suddenly could not stand to is telling, and it took me a while to piece it together\\. And then it took even longer for me to work out what that meant on a larger scale than me just being in some weird snit\\.\n> I dunno, this was kind of more just… stuff I wanted to say/clarify/explain more, but didn’t know where else to put it?\n> And I’m sorry if I didn’t go about this the best way\\. I thought maybe the airing of grievances \\(a festivus tradition\\!\\) would fix things, I figured it was just things bothering me or me being overly sensitive\\. But I dunno, man\\. I guess maybe it is just time for a break, be it permanent or temporary, to get some space and some air and some sense of ourselves or whatever, I really don’t know\\. I don’t really understand why something falls apart so suddenly after so long, even if I know it has been kinda donked up forever? And I kind of feel guilty, like I’m giving up on things? Which is silly, and which is also why I think I am so intent on stressing how possible I think it is that we just need a break from being a couple\\. Like\\. Not that it has to be just that\\. Maybe it is forever\\. But I think, for my own sake, it is important to say that it doesn’t have to be forever, either\\.\n> \n> Sorry\\. I feel like the end got very stream of conscious and loop\\-y\\. I have, as you may or may not be aware, never actually done this before, hah\\. 😕\n\nAlright, this is a lot, but I guess I only have a few specific things to say\\.\n\n- As far as the house thing goes, we’re talking about a massive, massive step, and expensive step today especially, and we’re talking about a step where we fundamentally disagree on a lot of the basics of it\\. I also think that, when you repeatedly press me on the house thing, it is out of self\\-interest\\. While I understand that, it is unfair to me, the person paying for the house\\.\n- But I mean\\.\\.\\. the rest? I think I agree with the rest\\.\n\nI\\.\\.\\.\nGoddammit\\. I don’t know how to even begin to do this kind of thing\\.\nI love you\\. I care about you\\. I respect you\\. I see you as an equal \\(no Morker how much you’ll often assert that I don’t\\)\\. I think we’ve both grown with and because of each other\\.\nBut I think you’re probably right \\- I think it really is a lot more of a friendship caring than a partnership caring\\.\nAnd I think we’ve probably got too much baggage\\. \n\nI mean\\.\\.\\. \nI could go back to my notes and I could talk about philosophy and roller blading and trying new foods and how much I’ve resented since childhood being told “just do it, you’ll have fun” when it’s not something I want to do\\.\nAnd I could talk about how I feel like everything is on me \\- because you’re not out doing things with other people, because you have no other outlet for things, all of that is on me, and whether you’re doing things or not doing things, enjoying things or not enjoying things\\.\\.\\. like\\. You isolate\\. And then it’s just me\\. Filling your social needs rests almost entirely on my shoulders\\. It has since, like, college\\.\nAll that to say\\.\\.\\. I think, when you talk about all this, when you talk about me not engaging you on Sims or not playing Don’t Starve with you or not roller skating with you\\.\\.\\. I think part of that is because I’m the only one there, and I don’t think that’s fair\\. To either of us, I suppose\\. But, like\\. It wouldn’t be nearly as big a deal if you had other outlets\\. But it’s just me\\. It’s almost always just been me\\.\n\nAnd\\.\\.\\. look, as long as we’re airing grievances, since I’m probably not going to get to it at this point since I don’t know that there’s a point in doing my whole “next set of notes” bit, the night we went roller skating was hell, absolute hell, and in hindsight, throwing me in the deep end was absolutely the wrong choice\\. You don’t start that cannoli in a crowded roller rink when the person has absolutely no experience with anything like it\\. \nSo when you talk about how I “refused to go roller skating with you”, it’s like, what, did you somehow have a completely different experience than I did? Was I not right on multiple levels about that? Was that night \\_really necessary\\_? Like, you’re calling me out for “not wanting to go roller skating with you” after I did and \\_that\\_ happened?\n\nAnd, I guess, while I’m thinking about it\\.\\.\\. you said “I appreciate you \\.\\.\\. calling me out for cannoli”\\. No you don’t\\. At least, not when it Morkers\\. Maybe after the fact, in a general sort of way, but not during the time period where you’re actually aware of what’s going on\\. Not in a way that \\*changes or improves things\\*\\. I’ve consistently felt like I was banging my head against a wall since college, so it\\.\\.\\. it really stands out to me when you say something like this\\. Sorry\\.\n\nSorry\\. I don’t really know how to do this\\. I don’t know how to go about this\\. I don’t even know how to admit to it\\.\n\nI don’t know\\.\nMaybe I’ll just go back through my notes and the original messages and see what I have left to say\\.\n\n- The specific items you listed about me making you “step out of your comfort zone” but refusing to “step out of my comfort zone” were all years old, and that’s important when we’re talking about things I look back on and am ashamed of\\.\n- The movie and theme park stuff we already covered, and as I said, I think I was an asshole high schooler for doing that and I should have been better, and you disagree fundamentally with that view\n- But I see it as a respecting boundaries thing I guess\\.\n- In general, what you’re seeing as “refusing to step out of your comfort zone”, I’m seeing as respecting boundaries and personal feelings\\.\n- The fireworks thing: Frodoe deal as the movies\\. It was something you did regularly, it was something you pushed for at least once, so for you to turn around, tell me you absolutely hated, \\_hated\\_ fireworks, and tell me off for somehow not knowing that about you, and use \\_that\\_ to prop up a larger point that I already kinda disagree with\\.\\.\\. that was a real “what the donk” moment\\.\n- Did I ever mention the Olive Garden in this conversation? That time I visited, I mentioned the Olive Garden, you didn’t want to, and then suddenly a few days later we’re going to the Olive Garden? It was fine that you didn’t want to\\. But, especially with all this context, it kinda feels like maybe you felt an obligation because of a lack of other things to do or something? And I don’t want you to feel that about things\\.\n- And then there’s things that you think I’m obligated to do\\.\n- Like the roller skating\\. Covered that above\\.\n- Asking after your sims \\- talked about that, don’t know how\\.\n\n- Trying foods \\- look, I can’t pretend to know how it feels to have a physical aversion to eating meat, but like\\. I also don’t think you can object if I suggest that \\_maybe, just maybe,\\_ I’m feeling similar things about other foods\\.\n- I’m a picky eater\\. I just am\\. It’s annoying, but I manage it, because I’m an adult who can manage things\\.\n- And while I understand, to some extent, that there’s a personal element to it because you love this stuff and want to share it\n- Sometimes I have a genuine physical revulsion to food\\. And some of that is stuff you eat\\. I hate to be this blunt, I’m sorry, but we’re talking about things where, in my eyes, they remind me of vomit or diarrhea or something\\. That’s just what they look like to me\\. And so no, they’re not going anywhere near my mouth\\.\n- And sometimes it’s not physical revulsion so much as knowing that, if that’s my meal, I’m going to be sitting at the dinner table all night, hating what I’m eating, hating that I’m stuck there\\. Because, you know, if I sit down to a meal, I’d like to enjoy myself\\.\n- And so, in the face of all that, I don’t think all this food stuff is really that important\\. I don’t get the importance of it\\. My diet isn’t ideal, it could stand to have more fruit and less junk in it, but, like\\.\\.\\. it’s not exactly the worst, most unhealthy thing in the world\\.\n- Why is it such a big deal? Why does it have to be such a personal insult when I don’t want to try something that looks gross to me? Why is that the hill to die on? Why is that a thing to hold up as “not making sacrifices for your partner”?\n\n- At some point, you wrote “you really need to take some time to sit down and think about what YOU want in the future”\n- And the reality is that I don’t know yet\\. And that’s kinda okay\\.\n- I want a place of my own and the time and space to figure out the next steps of my life\\.\n- What I do know is that the things I want, or don’t want, or am not ready to commit to, are often in direct conflict with the things you want, and I don’t know how to resolve that\\.\n- I want an apartment\\-style condo, not a house right now\n- I’m not ready for a pet or marriage or kids, and I’m \\_certainly\\_ not ready to even \\_think\\_ about the idea of adoption\\. That’s entirely outside of anything I’m comfortable with right now\\.\n- And I definitely disagree about homeschooling\\.\n- And I don’t know how to deal with that, to resolve that, because I don’t want to steamroll over the things you want\\. But it would be stupid of me to say:\n- “okay, fine, she wants a house with a yard, we’ll get one even though I’m not ready\\.”\n- “She wants a dog, we’ll get one even though I’m not ready\\.”\n- “She wants to adopt a kid, making me a father, ok, I can’t really say no to that, guess I’m a Regis now”\n- So we’re at an impasse, because I can’t rush things and toss opinions and uncertainties aside just because of things that you want\n- So I’m stuck\\. Multiple ways, multiple contexts\\.\n\nOkay, that was the cliff notes version of the last of my bullets from\\.\\.\\. Jan 2nd\\.\nSo now I’m just gonna skim your original messages and what I wrote in response\\.\n\n- The general overarching stuff, about me not putting in enough effort, about the friend vs romantic partner, etc\\., I’m inclined to concede and agree with\\.\n- \\.\\.\\.I guess that’s it\\. Just about all the specifics are covered at this point, and I’m really just left with\\.\\.\\. yeah\\. In general, I’m not a great partner to you\\.\n\nI\\.\\.\\.\\. yeah\\. I want space too, I think\\. I think there’s a strong argument for “we’re not actually all that great a couple”, I think there’s a strong argument for “our goals are unaligned and contradictory”\\. I think there’s a strong argument for “we’d be better off alone for a while, and then with other people”\\.\n\nI just\\.\\.\\. I don’t know\\. I don’t know how to do this, or what it entails\\.\nAnd I mean\\.\\.\\. well, in the past, the idea of breaking up with you has had a lot of guilt and fear attached to it\\.\nBut I don’t think I’m feeling that here, in context, with how well you’ve worked through everything\\.\nI just\\.\\.\\. don’t\\.\\.\\. I don’t know how to approach this\\. What to do about it\\. If we do it, if we go through with this, if we break up, it’ll probably be a while before I tell anyone\\. I don’t know how\\.\n\nI’m sorry\\.\n\n---\n\n11:00am\nI guess it’s good that I left this for today, when I had the time and space to be alone with it\\.\n\nI think I just need to send this\\.\nI can throw some extra stuff in if I think of anything\\.\n\n\\.\\.\\.\n\nAlright, it’s done\\."
